/*
 * lib/opcodes/SLOpArrget.sleela
 * SLeeLa Standard Library Definition.
 * Definition: Defines SLOpArrget, the single-opcode class for OP_ARRGET (canonical code 99).
 *
 * This class carries exactly ONE opcode: OP_ARRGET.
 * Semantics: pop an index then an array; push the element.
 * Membership: array extension (syntax 1.4) of the canonical SLeeLa ISA (lib/vm/InstructionSet.sleela).
 *
 * step() honours the family contract: it first calls the VM to advance to the
 * next instruction, then executes precisely this one opcode and returns the
 * next instruction pointer for the following opcode object.
 *
 * Family: opcodes. Native VM/OS work crosses an explicit bridge.
 */
#sleela 1.3
// Unified SLeeLa standard-library front-end object.
class SLOpArrget extends SLOpcodeBase {
  static final int CODE = 99;
  static final String MNEMONIC = "OP_ARRGET";

  void prepare() { configure(CODE, MNEMONIC); }
}
